FerrionOS change to base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f with ferrion-boot-splash.patch, ferrion-lockdown.patch, ferrion-pty-hangup.patch, ferrion-live-disk-view.patch, ferrion-sigchld.patch, ferrion-signal-handle-perm.patch and ferrion-rand-seed.patch applied (security roadmap S12, driver namespaces). Drivers enter the null namespace (memory and pipe) once they hold their handles:
- ihdad, nvmed, usbscsid, virtio-gpud, usbhidd, pcid, inputd, rtcd, redoxerd, usbhubd and usbctl's port command call setrens(0, 0) after their last open by path. ihdad opens its shared-memory directory /scheme/shm/audiohw at start and creates the audio ring in it, so the ring's name is audiohw.audio_shm. usbhidd enters it after its first HashMap, which opens the random scheme. rtcd opens the kernel's time offset before it reads the clock. redoxerd enters it after it has started its command.
- inputd opens a display's VT through the control handle the display driver sent it instead of by path, and driver-graphics answers an open on that control handle as it answers one on its root.
- fbcond and fbbootlogd enter the null namespace with setrens(0, 0) instead of setns(0), and audiod closes the namespace handle setns returns, so none of them holds its previous namespace handle.
- pcid-spawner, hwd and xhcid keep their namespace: the drivers they start register their schemes in the namespace they inherit, and a forked namespace is a copy, so those schemes would not appear in the one every other process uses.
- The namespace manager answers fpath on a namespace handle with `namespace:hardware=<0|1>;schemes=<names>;`, the schemes that handle can open, so /scheme/sys/iostat shows each process's namespace.

